            "text": "Hosfu is built around one practical rule: keep ordinary plastic away from the milk-contact path wherever possible.",
            "button_label": "See How Hosfu Fixes It",
            "microcopy": "Free shipping this week · 90-day money-back guarantee"
          }
        },
        "reason-4": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "4",
            "title": "It is not just one feed. It can repeat with daily washing and sterilising.",
            "body": "<p>A bottle is not used once. It is washed, sterilised, warmed, cooled, packed, dropped, scrubbed and reused again. Tiny scratches and repeated heat exposure are exactly why parents are starting to think beyond “is this bottle new?” and ask “what is this bottle made of?”</p><p>Plastic may look clean after every wash. But clean-looking and inert are not the same thing.</p>",
            "image": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0979/5082/6776/files/4_15b19733-c416-450a-9d2e-45308f304c8a.png?v=1783484878",
            "image_alt": "Daily washing and sterilising baby bottles"
          }
        },
        "reason-5": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "5",
            "title": "Even some “glass” bottles still put plastic where it counts",
            "body": "<p>Switching to glass feels like the obvious answer — until you look at the full milk path. Some bottles have a glass body, but still use plastic collars, vents, rings or bases that can sit near warm milk or steam during feeding and sterilising.</p><p>That is why Hosfu focuses on the entire system, not just the bottle body. A safer-feeling material on the outside does not help much if the feed still passes through ordinary plastic parts.</p>",
            "image": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0979/5082/6776/files/5_ef7f9eee-cb3d-4694-9a5a-75b44d15c0a1.png?v=1783484878",
            "image_alt": "Glass bottle comparison with plastic parts"
          }
        },
        "reason-6": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "6",
            "title": "Hosfu was designed around the milk-contact path",
            "body": "<p>Most bottle pages talk about shape, size and cute colours. Hosfu starts with a more serious question: <strong>what touches the milk when the bottle is warm?</strong></p><p>The Hosfu design is built around borosilicate glass and soft silicone for the surfaces that matter most, with heat-resistant components selected for daily sterilising routines. The goal is not to make feeding complicated — it is to remove the material guesswork from a routine parents repeat every day.</p>",
            "image": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0979/5082/6776/files/6_61353016-18f1-4e83-a3d0-2fc686ec4d21.png?v=1783484879",
            "image_alt": "Hosfu bottle materials and components overview"
          }
        },
